{{also|futtern|Füttern}}
==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈfʏtərn/|[ˈfʏtɐn]}}
* {{audio|de|De-füttern.ogg}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|de|gmh|vüetern}}, from {{inh|de|goh|fuotiren}}, derived from {{m|goh|fuotar}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*fōdrą|t=fodder}}. Equivalent to {{suffix|de|Futter|-n}}. Compare {{cog|nl|voeren|t=to feed}}, dialectal {{m+|en|to [[fodder]]}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|de|futtern||obsolete in this sense}}

====Verb====
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[feed]] {{gloss|to give food to}}
#: {{usex|de|die Vögel mit Sonnenblumenkernen füttern|inline=1}}
#: {{usex|de|den Vögeln Sonnenblumenkerne füttern|t=to feed sunflower seeds to the birds|inline=1}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The word is used chiefly with animals or otherwise when someone raises the food directly to another person’s mouth (e.g. that of a small child). For “to provide food” in general the usual word is {{m|de|ernähren}}.

=====Conjugation=====
{{de-conj}}

