===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|de|gmh|vüetern}}, derived from {{m|gmh|vueter}}, from {{der|de|goh|fuotar}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*fōdrą|t=sheath, wrapping, lining}}. Equivalent to {{suffix|de|Futter|-n}}. Compare {{cog|nl|voeren|t=to line}}. Probably remotely related to etymology 1, but not identical.

====Verb====
{{de-verb}}

# to [[line]] {{gloss|to cover the inner surface of a garment or bag}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{de-conj}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|de|ausfüttern}}
* {{l|de|unterfüttern|t=to undergird}}

